Package: CellHet
Title: Analysis of Cell Type Heterogeneity in Single-Cell Data
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2025-05-06
Authors@R: 
    person("Kai", "Guo", email = "guokai8@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")
           )
Description: A comprehensive toolkit for analyzing cell type heterogeneity in 
    single-cell RNA-seq data across multiple experimental conditions. 
    'CellHet' provides an integrated framework for differential expression analysis, 
    pathway enrichment, multi-modal data integration, and visualization of 
    cell type-specific responses. Key features include: identifying differentially 
    expressed genes across cell types and conditions, quantifying cell type response 
    heterogeneity, visualizing shared and unique molecular signatures using UpSet plots, 
    performing pathway enrichment analysis with multiple annotation databases, 
    integrating multi-modal data (RNA, protein, chromatin), analyzing gene expression 
    trajectories, and exporting results in publication-ready formats. The package 
    supports both Seurat and SingleCellExperiment objects, with parallel processing 
    capabilities for large datasets.
